text:
I’ll be sure to read what you write;

For I will love it, if your lines rhyme,

If they fall with rhythm and fit well with time!

When you see my wife
She does the housework with her pride;
Then she takes a seat by our fire
And she turns away from the fire.

" Sit down 'ere wid yer feet up high ;

Me hand be as warm as mayby."

John and his children are gone off to school;

Mayy has only one thing to do;

A pair o' shoes to bleach
Is on her list each week.

I never knowed what it meant, but now that I am
married,
If there's any house work done in this old

Thou who art God and knowest,
 My soul's despairing doubt;

 Thou canst not be mine, O Lord !
 But thou are my light and way ;

I don’t have any special talents;

I am just an ordinary man;

But my soul is full of wisdom;

My life has been a great lesson plan;

Through all these experiences, it taught me how

To love myself, others and even strangers too;

If I were born today, again would I live this way?

Of course I will – because now I have discovered the best things about humanity.

A beggar came along one day;
But there were no jobs for anyone there.
His name was Jim and he had only rags.
